s and their families are  going to benefit  from clean growth having a biden harris  administration  in the u.s provides that you know  friendly  almost competition to be able to seize  the opportunities that  this low-carbon economy sector  represents  canada faces homegrown challenges in  going green as a major carbon producer  but the change in washington like  biden's plan to rejoin the paris climate  agreement  is refocusing much of the world above  all climate change boris johnson seems  more than ready for joe biden he wants  to  join us next year in  leading the world in getting global  greenhouse emissions down as the world  takes new steps to reduce carbon  emissions  it also welcomes america's re-engagement  on climate change  eric sorensen global news toronto  americans urged to stay home for  thanksgiving coming up the serious  warning of aggressive and  unrelenting community spread  a week before american thanksgiving and  the u.s centers for disease control  is finally telling people to stay home  big gatherings will add fuel to what's  already a raging fire  there are now an average of 160 000 new  cases  every day in the u.s hospitalizations  have hit an all-time high nearly 80  thousand  and yesterday over 1800 americans died  jackson proskow on the latest  projections of where the u.s is headed  in their first public briefing since  july members of the white house  coronavirus task force painted a grim  picture this is more cases more rapidly  than what we had seen before  since the last task force briefing  another 120 thousand americans have died  this internal white house document shows  the areas with the highest rate of cases  and warns of aggressive unrelenting  community spread across the entire  country  i believe the day is coming soon when we  will put this coronavirus in the past  the surge in cases is so rapid the  centers for disease control is warning  americans not to travel for the  thanksgiving holiday  typically the busiest travel time of the  year when you have so much virus  circulating in the community everybody  needs to do their part to  stay home unless it's absolutely  necessary it's necessary to go out  in idaho doctors warn they'll soon face  tough choices about who they can treat  as they face a dire shortage of hospital  beds we may be  facing that scenario  in december the mayo clinic reports 900  of its staff have contracted the virus  in the past  two weeks the situation risks spiraling  out of control in multiple states  but not everyone is on board with public  health measures all they're trying to do  is  control you everything you do is based  on the mask and the disease  and it's wrong in south dakota where the  positivity rate is one of the highest in  the world  the governor refuses to implement a mask  mandate i don't want to approach a  policy or a mandate  just looking to make people feel good  experts say that lack of a unified  national response is what makes the  prolonged silence from the white house  so dangerous  at a time when the u.s needs leadership  the most it's been hard to find  donna okay jackson prosco in washington  thanks  ahead hospitals in europe close to the  breaking points  much of europe is in the grip of a  second wave of covid19 now the world  health organization says europe now  accounts for 28 percent of cases in the  world and  26 of all deaths crystal gomencing  reports  intensive care units in switzerland are  at capacity  geneva university hospital is shuttling  patients  to other facilities  the hospital director says we are still  in a situation that puts the health care  system  under a lot of pressure and they're not  alone  icus in france have been at 95 percent  capacity  for the past 10 days spain and italy are  also seeing more  critically ill patients last week  europe registered over 29 000  new covet 19 deaths that is  one person dying every 17 seconds  in the european region dr hound's clue  is urging people to stick with  protective measures  your country community family and  friends  need you like they have never needed you  before  he says only about 60 percent of the  european population  is wearing a mask in a move that could  increase numbers spain's health minister  reduced the price of face coverings  to 62 cents with transmission rates out  of control  millions of people are living with  restrictions  england should be moving out of lockdown  on december 2nd  but christmas could change that there's  talk  household mixing might be allowed over  the holidays  but that could extend the lockdown into  january  saying to families you can have a you  know a reasonably normal family  christmas  but then putting restrictions in place  which may well impact their livelihoods  i don't think he's going to be a very  welcome christmas present  right now a third of european countries  are reporting  very high infection rates of more than  700 cases  per 100 thousand people crystal  commansing global news  london up next an unexpected traveler in  the time  of covid  when i got started in tv news i thought  it was a bit silly to put cute animal  stories at the end of the news well  i'm much older now and covered in  everything so  now i crave cute animal stories the one  tonight is not a partridge in a pear  tree but  it's close this tiny owl was found stuck  inside the rockefeller center christmas  tree in new york city a construction  worker spotted it  rescued it put it in a cardboard box and  it's now recovering at a wildlife rehab  center  it's a northern sawet the smallest owl  in north america  workers say they did check the tree for  wildlife before they wrapped it but they  didn't spot the little owl  it went three days with no water or food  but it's now had a buffet  of mice and is said to be doing well  it's been named  rockefeller and it's outshining the  christmas tree itself which let's face  it looks a little  ragged new yorkers say it's a metaphor  for 2020 and that is global national for  this thursday i'm donna friesen  tonight's your canada is lilliwette bc  we'd love to see your canada please send  it to viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  bye
 

